course: dictionary
lesson: 821
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives two meanings for believer, and the sentence around it tells you which one is meant. Look for clues: is the sentence about a god or a religion, or about how strongly someone thinks something is good?
explain: «Christians believe the Holy Spirit is God present with and in believers.» Here believers are people who believe in God. This is the first meaning: someone who believes in a god or a religion.
explain: «Mum is a great believer in eating vegetables.» No god is mentioned here. A great believer means someone who strongly thinks something is true or good, so the second meaning fits. Test it: swap in "someone who strongly thinks vegetables are good for you" and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A believer is someone who believes in a god or a religion, or someone who strongly thinks something is true or good.
fact: «Believers» is the plural form, meaning more than one believer.
fact: The phrases a believer in, a great believer and a firm believer all show that someone feels strongly about an idea.
fact: A non-believer is someone who does not believe in a god or a religion.
fact: «Believers of different faiths» means people who follow different religions, and the sentence tells us they should respect each other.
exercise: «Baptist churches baptise believers by full immersion.» In this sentence, what does believers mean? | *People who believe in God and follow a religion | Fish that live in churches | People who strongly think vegetables are good | People who sing very loudly
exercise: «My grandad is a firm believer in early bedtimes.» What does believer mean here? | A person who wakes up very early | A sleepy person who yawns a lot | Someone who believes in a god | *Someone who strongly thinks early bedtimes are good
exercise: What is a non-believer? | A person who tells lies | *Someone who does not believe in a god or a religion | Someone who wants to become a believer | Someone who strongly thinks something is true
test: «Many believers say faith is trust, not proof.» What do these believers say faith is? | *Trust | A game | Proof | Money
test: Which phrase means someone who feels very strongly that something is good? | a believers' meeting | *a firm believer | a non-believer | a believer of different faiths
exam: «Dad is a great believer in walking to school.» What is the best meaning of believer here? | Someone who believes in a religion | A person who walks to school every day | *Someone who strongly thinks something is true or good | A person who does not believe in anything
